# Pairs with AllocatorAboveOrphans. Issue #5799's activation-recovery case: a
# new activation of the WAL shard re-seeds its allocator from the store alone,
# beneath its predecessor's flushes still in motion.
MODULE: AllocatorAboveOrphansRecoveryIgnoresPredecessor
TARGET: AllocatorAboveOrphans
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: activation recovery re-seeds from the store, beneath the predecessor's calls in motion
PERTURBS: ShardRecover

--- FIND
    /\ resyncing = "recover"
    /\ next' = ReseedNext
--- REPLACE
    /\ resyncing = "recover"
\* MUTATION: re-seed from the store alone.
    /\ next' = RecoveredNext
--- END
